1
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:10,900
Don't lay a finger on those
dice, Josuke Higashikata!

2
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:15,880
I would stay put if I were you.

3
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:21,080
I wonder what he's gonna do if he finds
out I've been cheating this whole time.

4
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:26,871
Well, let's just say a simple apology
won't be enough to smooth things over.

5
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:30,240
What exactly is the problem?

6
00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:35,680
It might be my mind playing tricks, but
I could swear the dice are staring at me.

7
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:44,020
Well, at any rate, let's
get back to the game.

8
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:49,880
Wow, you're way braver than I am.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:51,471
It'll just be two for me.

10
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:54,780
Catch my drift now, Mr. Alien?

11
00:00:55,560 --> 00:01:00,442
I know the point is to come out on top,
but I only have to do that by a little bit.

12
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:01,800
All right, go!

13
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:09,565
It's like what I'm saying is going
in one ear and out the other!

14
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:15,004
Guess that's what you
call a streak of luck, eh?

15
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:21,071
Rolling that score again isn't impossible.

16
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:25,640
An omen is worth five
times the initial bet, yes?

17
00:01:26,380 --> 00:01:27,320
Here you go.

18
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:29,484
The dice will roll as they may.

19
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:32,820
Guess so.

20
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:36,454
You can never predict these
kinds of things, am I right?

21
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:53,017
Let's break down, break down.

22
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:55,977
Let's break down, break down.

23
00:01:56,060 --> 00:01:58,737
Break down, break down.

24
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:00,160
Let's go.

25
00:02:56,813 --> 00:03:02,337
Meguru yuki de ikiru Match...

26
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:04,620
Nakedos!

27
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:27,117
You're insufferable.

28
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:28,057
However, for Mr.

29
00:03:28,140 --> 00:03:31,917
Joestar and Koichi's sakes, I've been
keeping my cool where you're concerned.

30
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,059
But that ends now.

31
00:03:33,220 --> 00:03:35,691
Cheating me crosses every line ever drawn.

32
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:40,497
I'm sure you've been gloating this entire
time, and the thought of it makes me sick.

33
00:03:40,580 --> 00:03:41,757
Just give me your hands.

34
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:43,577
I'll have Shining Diamond fix it for you.

35
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:44,601
Shut your mouth!

36
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:48,900
Do you have any idea why I
did that to my little finger?

37
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:53,797
So you can't back out of the game
like a coward, Josuke Higashkata!

38
00:03:53,880 --> 00:03:56,320
You're just a pea-brained dullard.

39
00:03:56,480 --> 00:03:59,245
I refuse to let you
disrespect the Great Rohan!

40
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:02,831
Each of us is going to have one more turn.

41
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:07,017
And as we play, I'll find a way to
see through your immoral deceptions.

42
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:11,120
But if I fail to uncover the truth
behind your clandestine tactics,

43
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:13,213
here's two million yen.

44
00:04:13,460 --> 00:04:15,857
Consider it monetary incentive to receive

45
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:18,646
treatment from Shining
Diamond after the game.

46
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:22,720
However, if I do unveil the
nature of your deception,

47
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:27,180
Your little finger will belong
to me, Josuke Higashikata.

48
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:29,890
Hey!

49
00:04:29,973 --> 00:04:33,095
Looks like you two are having
a rip-snortin' good time!

50
00:04:34,860 --> 00:04:36,680
Yo! Josuke! What's up?

51
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:38,120
Long time no see.

52
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:41,597
I've been stuck in that stupid
hospital for a month now.

53
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:43,717
I'm still kind of fuzzy on the details,

54
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:47,094
but I'm told I conked my
noggin on the side of the road.

55
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:48,110
Tamami?

56
00:04:48,193 --> 00:04:50,157
What the heck are you poking
your nose around here for?

57
00:04:50,240 --> 00:04:54,300
I hired him to be a repo man
of sorts, just as a precaution.

58
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:55,700
Repo man?

59
00:04:56,240 --> 00:05:00,160
Sorry to keep you boys waiting,
but I'm here and ready to serve.

60
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:03,000
And not to worry, I'm prepared.

61
00:05:03,480 --> 00:05:08,080
My trusty solar fixing lock will
ensure you receive what we agreed on.

62
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:13,560
I will fulfill my duty regardless of
who the victor is, you have my word.

63
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:17,637
My fees, whichever is the
greatest, Quee or 20%.

64
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:19,880
You'll both play one more round,

65
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:23,337
while Rohan tries to figure out how
you're cheating him, isn't that right?

66
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:24,250
Yes.

67
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:25,430
What?!

68
00:05:25,513 --> 00:05:26,343
Although,

69
00:05:26,426 --> 00:05:29,497
there's a chance you could be
tempted to withhold your trick,

70
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:32,260
so I will simply ensure that you don't.

71
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:35,817
Should you win without
your usual deceptions,

72
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:40,194
Tamami's lock will activate and
automatically attach itself to your body.

73
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:42,700
Now I'm really up shit creek.

74
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:44,320
It's now or never.

75
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:48,466
I've got to pull off this trick
and get myself out of this mess

76
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:51,180
If we're clear, I'll roll first.

77
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:52,210
Get ready

78
00:05:57,140 --> 00:05:58,280
Here it comes

79
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:01,420
A four!

80
00:06:01,740 --> 00:06:03,340
Two threes and a four

81
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:07,960
Thank God a normal result for once.

82
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,689
He won't figure it out now

83
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:15,080
So, it's my turn now, right?

84
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:18,817
Seems like a weight's been
lifted off your shoulders.

85
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:22,900
It's almost as though a task you
requested if someone was a success.

86
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:24,780
Just stay calm.

87
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:26,897
Rohan still doesn't have a clue.

88
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:28,220
I can do this.

89
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:34,737
What in the...

90
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:36,740
Is that barf?

91
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:38,737
Oh shit, he's getting dizzy.

92
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:41,800
I bet it's because Rohan
was shaking him so much.

93
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:43,180
Not so fast.

94
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:45,538
I insist you stop covering the dice.

95
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:49,177
I can't see them if they're
in your hand like that.

96
00:06:49,260 --> 00:06:51,319
Shake the dice with your palm open.

97
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:54,830
Huh?

98
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:56,440
Must be a fire somewhere.

99
00:06:59,080 --> 00:06:59,910
What?

100
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:01,310
Sirens?

101
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:03,470
That's right.

102
00:07:03,740 --> 00:07:05,916
He's allergic to the sound of sirens.

103
00:07:06,160 --> 00:07:08,631
At this rate, he'll revert back to normal.

104
00:07:08,820 --> 00:07:10,120
What is the hold-up?

105
00:07:10,300 --> 00:07:11,397
Quit your stalling!

106
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:13,892
Show me what you're holding in your hand!

107
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:14,830
Aaaaaaah!

108
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:17,897
You just heard the way I get
myself hyped up for battle!

109
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:19,440
Now get ready to lose!

110
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:21,160
Do it! Go!

111
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,940
It's a 6-6-6 Hamon!

112
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:33,777
And the lock didn't activate!

113
00:07:33,860 --> 00:07:35,919
Josuke's a low-down rotten cheater!

114
00:07:37,940 --> 00:07:39,100
So how about it?

115
00:07:39,280 --> 00:07:41,398
Did you figure it out, Rohan-sensei?

116
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:48,617
Well, what's the word?

117
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:51,582
Does your silence mean
you throw it in the towel?

118
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:55,617
Looks like those weird little
dots aren't on Rohan's side.

119
00:07:55,700 --> 00:07:56,660
Hang in there.

120
00:07:57,780 --> 00:07:59,657
Oh, don't leave us here in suspense!

121
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:01,446
Did you figure it out or not?

122
00:08:06,340 --> 00:08:11,100
Of course it all makes sense
Damn, I'm toast I've got it!

123
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:12,860
The fire's here!

124
00:08:13,980 --> 00:08:16,717
Rohan Sensei, your house
is burning to the ground.

125
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:19,957
It was the magnifying glass.

126
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:22,137
The sunlight went through
it and started the fire.

127
00:08:22,220 --> 00:08:24,396
We were distracted and didn't notice.

128
00:08:25,060 --> 00:08:25,920
Shut up!

129
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:28,877
I don't care if the house
ends up in a heap of ash All

130
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:31,517
that matters here is figuring
out how Josuke's cheating!

131
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:32,776
Don't be ridiculous!

132
00:08:32,940 --> 00:08:35,517
Just take your two million
and get the hell out of here!

133
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:37,600
Well, I think I'll be going now.

134
00:08:37,840 --> 00:08:38,900
Hey, come back!

135
00:08:39,140 --> 00:08:41,905
But before I go, I'll
fix that finger of yours!

136
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:44,877
Oh, you can't just heal
people without permission!

137
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:45,790
Josuke, wait!

138
00:08:46,060 --> 00:08:47,100
You bastard!

139
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:51,120
That was a close one.

140
00:08:51,380 --> 00:08:54,877
I guess I'm the kind of guy that
some people just love to hate, huh?

141
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:56,195
Who would've figured?

142
00:08:56,620 --> 00:08:57,450
What's wrong?

143
00:08:57,533 --> 00:08:58,363
You seem displeased.

144
00:08:58,446 --> 00:09:01,097
Tell me, was I of adequate
assistance to you?

145
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:03,480
Could you like... Shut up! Jeez!

146
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:05,720
Rohan Kishibe's house.

147
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:08,802
Half burned and seven
million yen in fire damage.

148
00:09:09,080 --> 00:09:11,157
Josuke may have escaped unscathed,

149
00:09:11,240 --> 00:09:15,005
but he managed to find himself
even further on Rohan's bad side.

150
00:09:21,220 --> 00:09:23,977
Just a friendly reminder
to all you drivers out

151
00:09:24,060 --> 00:09:26,297
there to be extra careful
when you're on the road.

152
00:09:26,380 --> 00:09:31,080
It seems a motorcycle crashed at the
entrance of Futatsumori Tunnel yesterday,

153
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:33,675
and the young rider was badly injured.

154
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:36,537
Police later discovered
that the accident...

155
00:09:36,620 --> 00:09:38,760
Mom's been acting different lately.

156
00:09:39,140 --> 00:09:42,280
She's been dressing up,
wearing new lipstick.

157
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:43,940
She's happy.

158
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:49,100
Did something happen?

159
00:09:54,080 --> 00:09:59,000
Interesting mom doesn't usually get
naked in front of dad not in that way.

160
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:06,995
Sometimes I wonder if I was born to
parents with no love for each other.

161
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:11,220
What's he doing?

162
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:19,540
Josuke, the guy's guitar, Jotaro, Kujo,
they're the reason I'm in this predicament.

163
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:31,320
Oh, Josuke, it's you.

164
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:32,641
Thank you again.

165
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:34,260
Hey man, no problem.

166
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:37,657
So did you find a place to
sleep and get a bite to eat?

167
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:39,020
Mikitaka! Mikitaka!

168
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:41,620
Get your hiney over here this instant!

169
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:44,017
We haven't been in town that long,

170
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:46,597
and there are lots of errands
to be done, young man.

171
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:50,260
Of course. Sorry, Mother.
I'm coming. Huh? Mother?

172
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:51,820
Oh, for Pete's sake.

173
00:10:52,060 --> 00:10:54,397
Are you telling people
that you're an alien again?

174
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:57,017
What have I told you about
playing these pranks?

175
00:10:57,100 --> 00:10:59,880
I do apologize if my
boy has been a bother.

176
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:03,317
They actually took him seriously
at his school in Tokyo.

177
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:05,871
You should have seen the ruckus he caused.

178
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:08,411
Now, if you'll excuse us.

179
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:10,630
What?

180
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:13,877
I brainwashed her, isn't that great?

181
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:15,901
As far as she knows, I'm her son.

182
00:11:16,500 --> 00:11:19,676
Mikitaka Hazekura is my alias
while I'm here on Earth.

183
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:21,100
So long for now.

184
00:11:21,660 --> 00:11:23,240
Mikitaka, it's time to go!

185
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:30,780
What the hell is going on here?

186
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:33,077
Just who the devil was that armball?

187
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:35,017
Was he serious about being an alien?

188
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:39,677
Or was he simply a stand user I created
when I threw the arrow and cut his neck?

189
00:11:39,760 --> 00:11:42,097
The way that boy was able
to drive a wedge between

190
00:11:42,180 --> 00:11:45,137
Josuke and Rohan was
certainly a sight of the hold.

191
00:11:45,220 --> 00:11:47,380
But, he's out.

192
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:50,197
Next they'll face the stand, Highway Kick.

193
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:52,221
It'll crush whoever hunts my son.

194
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:13,622
Are you just going to ignore me?

195
00:12:13,860 --> 00:12:15,877
The least you could do is say hello.

196
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:20,660
It's common courtesy to address those
older than you, Josuke Higashikata.

197
00:12:23,460 --> 00:12:24,754
Sorry about yesterday.

198
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:28,480
So, uh, that fire was
crazy, wasn't it? Yes.

199
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:32,117
That was approximately 2.5
million yen worth of furniture.

200
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:35,017
Those pieces were used in the
movie Pretty Woman, you know.

201
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:37,460
Not that any of that bothers me.

202
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:39,770
What?

203
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:40,880
Have a seat.

204
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:50,340
Mark my words, I'll repay you for
yesterday's game one way or another.

205
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:58,557
That was...

206
00:12:58,640 --> 00:12:59,917
Josuke, did you see that?

207
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,765
There was a door to a
house in the tunnel wall.

208
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:03,980
Someone's inside.

209
00:13:06,600 --> 00:13:07,580
It's a window.

210
00:13:07,820 --> 00:13:09,937
There's a room beyond these tunnel walls.

211
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:12,844
And from what I can see,
someone's living in it.

212
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,038
There's a man, too.

213
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:17,860
But I can't see their faces.

214
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:20,200
What is he attempting to do?

215
00:13:28,860 --> 00:13:31,120
Josuke, tell me you saw that. Enough!

216
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:32,597
I've had it with you.

217
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:35,151
Don't think you can screw with me forever.

218
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:39,760
No one else can see the room.

219
00:13:43,540 --> 00:13:46,100
Is that house a new stand user?

220
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:51,520
The man who cut off that woman's
hand, could he be Yoshikage Kira?

221
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:09,649
You expect me to believe there
was a room inside the tunnel?

222
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:11,449
You're not fooling anyone.

223
00:14:11,780 --> 00:14:14,956
Is that half-baked lie your
way of getting back at me?

224
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:16,820
So you have no faith in me.

225
00:14:17,060 --> 00:14:18,648
Is that what you're saying?

226
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:21,800
That's rich coming from
a cheater like you.

227
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:26,037
And not only are you a cheater, you're
a cheater who lies to cover his tracks.

228
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:28,473
You have the gall to accuse me of lying?

229
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:31,637
Well, I should have known we
would never see eye to eye.

230
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:35,485
You wouldn't understand even if
I took you back there to see it.

231
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:40,880
All right, let's do this.

232
00:15:01,700 --> 00:15:03,300
The exit...

233
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:10,360
There's nothing here.

234
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:14,188
I could have sworn there was
something, but it's just a wall.

235
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:16,000
So it was an illusion.

236
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:19,630
What?

237
00:15:23,140 --> 00:15:24,857
Wait, this is...

238
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:26,881
It's the room I saw from the bus.

239
00:15:31,980 --> 00:15:33,917
He just appeared out of thin air.

240
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,294
But what happened to the man
and woman who were in here?

241
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:48,350
Blast it!

242
00:15:48,433 --> 00:15:49,497
Something's in there!

243
00:15:49,580 --> 00:15:52,000
This room is a trap and I fell for it!

244
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:55,995
Whatever's in there is getting closer.

245
00:15:56,180 --> 00:15:58,827
I don't see a thing,
but something is coming!

246
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:05,297
that wouldn't have ended
well it was totally

247
00:16:05,380 --> 00:16:07,617
invisible but something was moving toward

248
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:14,020
me something non-human that room was bait
and the cure-looking Fool was an illusion

249
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:17,897
there's no doubt in my
mind that room is a stand

250
00:16:17,980 --> 00:16:20,820
going it alone is risky
i should tell mr joestar

251
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:24,280
Damn it!

